#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026e9975-ba0c-5eae-815a-fcd1e665b3d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542645} {:answer/id #uuid "79ac5216-69de-5dc4-a92b-b636df49e5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542962} {:answer/id #uuid "7f21a217-b4f0-55ce-b377-f084a5b14d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542982} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c913d4-93f7-5765-8bb6-090f7d52622b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543150} {:answer/id #uuid "e014b07e-27e4-516d-adc5-1ef689408d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ac5216-69de-5dc4-a92b-b636df49e5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542962} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c3c93af-58f9-530c-baad-0a629ae81ede" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e0723ce-a987-5c3e-a185-24b9f3aa7c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95270" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $3\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nII. Any $8\\times 6$ matrix $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $8\\times 6$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $6\\times 8$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $6\\times 6$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{6\\times 8}\\times {A}_{8\\times 6}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{6\\times 6}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $6$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have a negative singular value.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d7b9b80-3654-5da0-af41-f1dd281a1ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9,\\,3,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404796} {:answer/id #uuid "adfd1028-f71d-5fb8-bf65-f6a904a4cad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404797} {:answer/id #uuid "421f5096-6ffe-58b8-95fd-205273c0d9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404798} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9e32e2-6234-54e2-a995-a9f7bc9f67fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404799} {:answer/id #uuid "b769f855-028a-56bf-bb0f-d1970e2ab6bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "421f5096-6ffe-58b8-95fd-205273c0d9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404798} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e48eb31-ad56-59b2-a6ab-bf3fcb90c449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de321704-9fad-5ba9-910c-dac492b8f0a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95377" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )[(8-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4)]+2(-2)(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4)+(-4)(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4-4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a190c4a-9cc2-50ab-a107-16fc3f92fc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3},\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415545} {:answer/id #uuid "1e594ce1-22ea-5fd6-afb9-6b06b4b9255c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415546} {:answer/id #uuid "70323d57-c32e-523a-902e-eb0de24ca0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415554} {:answer/id #uuid "83f12e6b-62c0-5595-a194-e0065cfb501d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415557} {:answer/id #uuid "c6eb0c7d-ecb7-57ee-81fb-a558588e214e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6eb0c7d-ecb7-57ee-81fb-a558588e214e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415564} :answer-field/id #uuid "646b1b63-2cd4-5c4d-b0e4-160d844e1954" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-95378" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =2,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
